      <div type="clause" n="47">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 47</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="47" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="344" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa openlice<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_47.lnote.oe.12"/> lengctenbryce gewyrce þurh feohtlac oððe þurh wiflac [oððe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_47.lnote.oe.star"/> þurh reaflac] oððe þurh ænige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_47.lnote.oe.13"/> healice misdæda<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_47.lnote.oe.14"/>, sy þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> twybete, swa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_47.lnote.oe.15"/> on heahfreolse, be ðam þe seo dæd<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_47.lnote.oe.3-2"/> si.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="47" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="344" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf hwa opendlice<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_47.lnote.oe.2"/> lencgtenbryce gewyrce ðurh feohtlac oððe ðurh wiflac oððe ðurh reaflac oððe ðurh ænige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_47.lnote.oe.3"/> healice misdæde, sy þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> twibote, swa [eac<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_47.lnote.oe.4"/>] on heahfreolse, be ðam ðe seo dæd sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="47" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="344" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hwa openlice lenctenbryce gewyrce þurh feohtlac oððe þurh wiflac oððe þurh reaflac oððe þurh ænige healice misdæde, sy þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> twybete, swa on heahfreolse, be þam þe seo dæde sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="47" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="345" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis aperte quadragesimale ieiunium frangat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_47.lnote.oe.6"/> per pugnam uel per concubitum aut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_47.lnote.oe.7"/> rapinam uel per<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_47.lnote.oe.8"/> aliquod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_47.lnote.oe.9"/> summorum criminum, sit hoc duplo corrigendum, sicut in summis festiuitatibus, secundum quod factum erit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="47" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="345" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis uiolauerit ieiunium quadragesimale<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_47.lnote.oe.6-2"/> aut pugnando aut rapiendo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_47.lnote.oe.7-2"/> aut mulierem ducendo aut aliquid mali magni faciendo, dupliciter emendet secundum emendationem operis uiolatę festiuitatis.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="47" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="345" ed="#liebermann"/>[47] Si quis manifeste quadragesimalem obseruacionem transgreditur siue sedicione siue nupciis siue rapina siue quoquam magnifico peccato, dupliciter hoc corrigatur secundum peccati modum, sic et in reuerenda solempnitate.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="47" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="200" ed="#robertson"/>Gyf hwa opendlice lencgtenbryce gewyrce ðurh feohtlac oððe ðurh wiflac oððe ðurh reaflac oððe ðurh ænige healice misdæde, sy þæt twibote<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_47.robnote.fn.1"/>, swa eac<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_47.robnote.fn.2"/> on heahfreolse, be ðam ðe seo dæd sy.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="280" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Gif hwa openlice lengctenbryce gewyrce þurh feohtlac oððe þurh wiflac oððe þurh reaflac oððe þurh ænige healice misdæda, sy þæt twybete, swa on heahfreolse, be ðam þe seo dæd si.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="344" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand unleugbar<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_47.lnote.de.1"/> Fastenbruch verübt durch Fechten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_47.lnote.de.2"/> oder durch Beischlaf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_47.lnote.de.3"/> oder<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_47.lnote.de.4"/> durch Räuberei oder durch irgend welche schwere Missethaten, sei das doppelt busspflichtig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_47.lnote.de.5"/>, wie (auch <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) am hohen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_47.lnote.de.6"/> Feiertag, je nachdem die That ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If anyone openly breaks the Lenten fast by fighting or by intercourse or by robbery or by any grave misdeed, let it be subject to double compensation, as (also, B) on a high feast-day, according to what the deed is.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_47.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="201" ed="#robertson"/>If anyone openly causes a breach of the fast of Lent by fighting or by intercourse with women or by robbery or by any great misdeed, he shall pay double compensation<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_47.robnote.n.2"/>, in accordance with the nature of the offence, just as he must do during a high festival.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IICn_47.whinote.n.4"/><pb n="469" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone openly commits a breach of the Lenten fast by fighting or intercourse with women or by robbery<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IICn_47.whinote.n.5"/> or by any other grave crime, double compensations are to be paid, as on a high festival, in proportion to the deed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="281" ed="#rabin-doml"/>If anyone openly violates the Lenten fast by fighting or engaging in illicit intercourse or by robbery or any serious crime, he shall pay a double penalty according to the seriousness of the offense, as is appropriate during a religious feast.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="344, 345"><ref target="clause:Af_5-5">Af 5.5</ref>; <ref target="clause:Af_40-1">Af 40.1f.</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">*Vgl. Af. 5, 5; 40, 1 f. | Vgl. Af. 5, 5; 40, 1 f.</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:Af_5-5">Af 5.5</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 47: Af 5:5,40:1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:Af_40-1">Af 40.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 47: Af 5:5,40:1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="469"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_5-5">Af 5.5</ref> <quote>c.f. Alfred 5.5, 40.1f.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="469"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_40-1">Af 40.1</ref> <quote>c.f. Alfred 5.5, 40.1f.</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">In G, ‘oððe þurh reaflac’ was written above the line in the 16th century; it was originally missing from Quadr. too. Liebermann compares Af 5.5; 40.1 f.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 345, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">oððe þurh reaflac: in a sixteenth-century hand over an erasure in G</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">swa on: swa eac on B</note>
